WEBVTT

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.580
<i>Man, the future really is here, isn't it?</i>

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.430
<i>That was today's look into the 
wild world of home appliances.</i>

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.520
<i>Tomorrow we'll look at the secrets
 of the sponge gourd</i>

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.190
<i>everyone seems to be talking about.</i>

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.450
<i>See you then.</i>

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.580
<i>That's it for tonight's </i>Evening File.<i></i>

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.890
<i>We'll see you tomorrow.</i>

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.460
Great work, everyone!

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:26.840
Great work.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.150
Kunieda-san, I'm so sorry!

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.960
That news flash script 
I gave you was a page short!

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.900
That's all right.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.200
The show still went on just fine.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.540
It just surprised me, is all. 
You didn't hear my voice crack?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.680
Not at all! You sounded great, as usual!

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.200
Then all's well that ends well.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.390
See you tomorrow.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.640
See you tomorrow!

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.150
<i>These stupid assholes don't have 
a goddamned clue what they're doin'!</i>

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.850
<i>This studio's staffed with incompetents.</i>

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:05.960
Yes, No, or Maybe?

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.920
Here's tomorrow's on-location script 
and subject dossier.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.490
Sorry it's so late.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.550
Not at all.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.720
Thank you so much.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:14.940
<i>You </i>better<i> be sorry!</i>

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.430
<i>You're always handin' your crappy 
scripts in at the last minute!</i>

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.520
<i>Incompetent!</i>

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.170
I'm interviewing an animator, then?

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:24.240
Yeah, he's doing the new 
opening for <i>The News</i>.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.360
Not sure why we need to 
do a story on it, personally...

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.360
It's all hands on deck for 
the show's renewal, I suppose.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.360
Asuo Keiichi is reinventing the nightly news.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.690
Our producer, Shitara-san, really does 
like arranging things, doesn't he?

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.590
The interviewee's a great guy, 
though. No worries.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.070
I'm glad to hear it.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.100
<i>"Newscaster" is a curious occupation.</i>

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.740
<i>You're on TV, so you're a bit like a celebrity,</i>

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.100
<i>but status-wise, you're a cog in a machine.</i>

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.650
<i>You can collect a good paycheck 
without selling yourself constantly,</i>

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.810
<i>but as long as you're on TV,</i>

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:14.770
<i>you have to refrain from activities 
that might turn the viewers against you.</i>

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.000
<i>But, look...</i>

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.070
<i>Sometimes I wanna thumb through the 
trashy mags at the convenience store,</i>

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.210
<i>or buy just 100 grams of pre-prepared meals 
at the department store grocery,</i>

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:27.790
<i>or clap back at a taxi driver 
who's mouthing off at me.</i>

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.710
<i>If I had to always keep on 
my newscaster face,</i>

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.820
<i>holding back on all those little things...</i>

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.300
<i>I'd suffocate and die.</i>

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.200
<i>I spend time as this almost 
sus-looking character</i>

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.770
<i>to let out all the stress 
"Kunieda Kei" can't.</i>

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.360
<i>The brief minutes I spend like this 
are a precious breath of fresh air.</i>

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.280
I'm droolin' here!

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.280
Time to dig in!

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.620
So good!

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.410
<i>Good evening. I'm News 
Network Broadcaster Aidawara.</i>

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.200
<i>A quick report on the shark 
found in Yodogawa, Osaka.</i>

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.140
<i>We have a reporter on scene. 
 Okehazama-san, over to you.</i>

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.040
<i>This is Okehazama here in Yodogawa.</i>

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.800
Better review that stuff, I guess.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.800
<b>Tsuzuki Ushio
</b>
Recent Works
ITORY, "Mineral Water Born in the Mountains" 
ITORY, "Tea Craft"
Shishin Food Products, "SIO Ramen" 
Kanai Pharmaceuticals, "E4 Premium Eyedrops"
KB Cosmetics, "FAKE" Brand ads
bv, "More Family Connections" series

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.800
Tsuzuki Ushio, huh?

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:35.330
Oh, it's one of these?

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:39.080
Move the model an inch, film it, 
then move it another inch...

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.280
What kind of weirdo likes doing that stuff?

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:45.400
<i>"Tsuzuki Ushio, 27 years old."</i>

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.940
<i>Same age as me, huh?</i>

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.550
<i>"Began making original stop-motion pieces 
while attending art school.</i>

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.000
<i>Streaming sites catapulted him 
to worldwide attention.</i>

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.210
<i>His animated short depicting 
a bird's life from hatching to death</i>

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.440
<i>racked up over ten million views."</i>

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.550
<b>Tsuzuki Ushio at Awards Ceremony</b>

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.720
Prettyboy, huh?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.300
<b>He is openly bisexual.</b>

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.640
What if he falls for me?

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.980
Kunieda Kei.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.630
Can you keep up the masquerade another day?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.530
<i>I thought this place looked familiar...</i>

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.660
<i>It's my neighborhood.</i>

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.660
<b>Saito Contractors</b>

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.920
<i>Wow, I wonder if we shop 
at the same stores...</i>

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.220
The first floor is his 
studio-slash-workshop.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.640
The second floor is where he lives.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:43.960
The front door is this way.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.180
You think he's asleep?

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:53.600
<b>Tsuzuki</b>

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.010
Hey.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.290
Good morning, Tsuzuki-san.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.280
We're very sorry to wake you.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.220
<i>This jerk!</i>

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.670
I really am sorry. 
I thought it was tomorrow.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.030
<i>Who does he think he's fooling 
with that yawning act?</i>

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.560
Oh, no! Didn't they call you yesterday?

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.560
<i>We freakin' </i>told you <i>when 
the interview was scheduled!</i>

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.470
Do I have time to wash up and change?

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.470
<i>Even if you're not gonna have tea prepared,</i>

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.230
<i>at least be waitin' like a proper adult!</i>

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.670
We'll get some exterior shots.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:16.270
Is it all right if Kunieda waits inside?

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.290
Sure.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.020
Oh, this is Kunieda. 
He'll be handling the interview.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.570
He's our secondary newscaster 
for <i>Evening File</i>.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.010
A pleasure. I'm Kunieda Kei.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.020
Let's have a great interview.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:29.980
Hey.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.720
I'll do my best to make it good, so—

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.160
Just do whatever.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.790
I'm sure you've got better things to do.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.390
I don't have a lot of time 
for cameras, either.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.980
I'm on a deadline, after all.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.440
<i>Yeah, right! "Great guy," my ass!</i>

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.070
Is it all right that I put my things there?

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.250
Go ahead.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.480
Do you handle all the work yourself?

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.010
No money for assistants.

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:06.920
<i>Yeah, I'll bet!</i>

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:08.940
That must be hard.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.780
Nah, I'm grateful just to be able
 to make a living doing it.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.970
I'm getting paid for my hobby, more or less.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.390
<i>Good on you for getting it!</i>

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:22.370
<i>Creators are always up their asses 
about how important they are...</i>

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.880
Tsuzuki-san, are you ready?

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.130
We'd like to get some footage 
of you in the studio, first.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:28.900
Sure thing.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:33.040
If there's anything you don't want 
on-camera, feel free to hide it.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.410
There's not.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:38.440
<i>Oh, hey... he can be kinda chill, too.</i>

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.900
<i>He should do that more oft—</i>

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.810
You idiot!

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:43.920
I'm sorry!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.110
Darn it...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.170
Japanese Pronunciation
Inflection
Dictionary

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:46.650
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:47.400
Are you all right?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.130
Kunieda-san... I'm so sorry.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.680
Really, it's nothing.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.530
<i>Damn klutz!</i>

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.180
You weren't hurt?

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.770
No... I'm so sorry.

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:00.270
What is it?

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.270
Oh... nothing—

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.400
Okay, let's get rolling!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.740
Sure!

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.950
<i>Crap! The nightly roundtable 
is about to start!</i>

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.280
<i>How could I have forgotten to tape it?</i>

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.990
<i>Asuo-san is moderating, 
so I can't afford to—</i>

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.670
That was close!

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.130
Oh, crap!

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.630
Thank goodness... it's intact.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:28.830
Hey!

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:30.490
You bastard...

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.410
You just leap out into the road,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.060
and your first concern is your damned food?!

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.790
<i>Oh, please. You're unscathed 
enough to bitch about it...</i>

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.400
Hey! You're not going anywhere!

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.730
Let me go, you—

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:48.350
Ow...

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:51.800
<i>Tsuzuki... Ushio?</i>

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.700
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.990
<i>He won't know you're Kunieda Kei.</i>

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.160
What's your problem, anyway?

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.350
C'mon, help me get my bike up!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.660
My hand hurts and feels stiff.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.800
I think you bent the frame...

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.050
How much do you want?

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.540
For the bike and 
the treatment for your hand.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.080
Hundred thousand? Two hundred thousand? 
Name your price.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.050
I can cover it.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.160
Look, I'm in a hurry!

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.140
You're in a hurry, so you can 
just ignore the light?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.130
I didn't ignore the light.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.440
It was green!

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:30.790
There're no cameras set up, 
and no other witnesses.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:32.820
So it's your word against mine.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.640
Just let me pay to fix—

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:38.090
Ow!

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.630
Ow! That hurt me, too, dumbass!

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.700
You made me use my injured hand...

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:44.670
What's wrong with you?!

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.950
Who in the world raised you?!

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.810
Why wasn't "I'm sorry" the first 
thing outta your mouth?!

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:54.220
Only trash can't manage 
a simple "thanks" or "sorry"!

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.530
My bad.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:57.890
You little...

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.030
I'll wallop you with my good hand this time!

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.190
Darn it...

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:05.910
Look. Help me walk the bike, would you?

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.290
My foot hurts, too.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:09.440
Fine...

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.320
I see your bag.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.540
The gyudon at Sudo-tei is pretty great, huh?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:29.230
The... broth, sauce, 
whatever you'd call it...

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.900
It's been different lately, right?

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.550
I hear you.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.970
They changed the ratio of sugar 
and soy sauce slightly.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.110
Right?

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.750
Do you eat it in?

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.180
Take-out only.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:45.520
I sometimes eat in, 
but their beer is the worst.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.340
Beer is the same everywhere.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:49.680
Hard disagree!

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:53.690
The head's totally run down 
by the time it reaches the table.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.580
I don't know if the pourer sucks at 
his job or the server is slow or what...

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.690
Feelings on yakitori?

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:01.560
Positive.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.400
Tanmi-ya behind the post office 
has the good stuff.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.380
Do they do take-out?

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.500
Heck yeah, they do!

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:14.260
That's cold!

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:17.560
Well, bye.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.260
Wait, hang on!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.520
What now?

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.550
We're not done yet!

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.250
By the way, why aren't you asking?

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.580
About what?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.960
About all the stuff I have lying around...

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.610
Aren't you curious about who I really am?

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.370
<i>I already know, stupid!</i>

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.610
No interest.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.030
I don't think it's about interest...

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.330
Ah, well.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:41.570
I make videos.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.200
I create everything by hand.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.510
And I just got a big contract which 
I'm in the middle of planning out.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.820
I'm even getting TV interviews about it.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:54.810
A disabled left hand is really 
going to set me back.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:58.220
So you should take some responsibility 
and help me for a while.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.020
No way.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.980
Are you really in a position to refuse?

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.870
I already told you I'd pay!

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.980
Get yourself a part-timer or something!

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.820
Always money, money, money...

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.340
Don't you feel ashamed of yourself?

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.660
Hell no!

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.320
Let's get this straight.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.880
I'm not a millionaire or anything!

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.230
I'm working my ass off all the damn time,

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.820
trying to make as much money as I can!

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.640
And I wanna use that money 
to take responsibility!

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.100
I guess you think that's wrong, huh?!

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:26.200
But I'm not one bit ashamed!

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:30.580
What now?

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.580
Well, you've got a point!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.340
You're a pretty convincing person, you know.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.970
Don't expect me to celebrate.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.100
What's your name?

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.980
Your name.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.430
I'm Tsuzuki.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.740
<i>I didn't think that far ahead...</i>

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.800
<i>A name... just make up a name...</i>

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:54.120
<i>If he's "Tsuzuki..."</i>

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.060
Owari.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:58.040
Wow, Owari?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.530
Tsuzuki, continuation... and Owari, ending...

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:03.290
They're kind of close. Or maybe not, huh?

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.530
What's your first name?

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.580
Why do you care?

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.760
Well, fair enough.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.610
Tomorrow night, come by for two hours.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.580
You can pick the time yourself.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.590
Did you hear what I said?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.090
Seriously, the job isn't hard.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.360
<i>Wait just a damn minute!</i>

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.060
You're an interesting guy.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:25.590
It'd be a shame to let things end like this.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.470
<i>No, let's end it!</i>

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.310
<i>I named myself "ending" for a reason, dude!</i>

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.510
I'll pay you a bit, too.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:32.350
How much?

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.460
How about a bowl of gyudon per day?

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.520
Cheap-ass...

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.580
See you tomorrow.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:42.190
Will not.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.920
I ain't comin', got it?

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:46.670
I ain't, got it?

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:50.070
I ain't comin'!

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:52.200
No way in hell am I comin'!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:53.370
<b>Tsuzuki</b>

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:55.710
Hey!

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:00.740
I left my gyudon here last night.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:01.870
I ate it.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:04.840
Thief!

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.370
What's this stuff?

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:14.250
I'm making an animation for 
the opening of a news program.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.100
<i>Tell me somethin' I don't know!</i>

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:21.110
I wanted to create a scene like 
the Shibuya Scramble Crossing.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:22.990
You're a masochist.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:24.770
I want you to paint them.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:25.480
Hell no!

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:28.070
Just paint them however 
you think looks best.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.150
So I can paint their faces green?

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.570
Do what you like, within reason.

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:35.970
When it's done, you'll 
be able to brag about it.

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:38.250
"I'm the one who painted that!"

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.420
Who'd brag about that?

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.800
<i>I'm already on TV plenty!</i>

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.570
Boy, my hand hurts...

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:49.020
They said it was a strain. 
It'll take two or three weeks to heal!

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:52.640
Dunno what'll happen 
if I miss my deadline...

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.500
The client's a TV station, after all...

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.630
I might be blacklisted from the industry!

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:00.690
I might even get fined 
for breach of contract!

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.940
Fine! I'm doin' it, already!

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:10.240
What? I'm not taking revisions.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.520
Actually, I'm impressed.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.410
You took it more seriously than I expected.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:16.970
What?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:19.700
A person's personality 
comes out in their work.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.920
More than they ever realize.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:26.780
You're a fast learner, 
you're smart, and you're quick.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:30.710
But despite your insistence, 
you did a proper coloring job.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.830
You're surprisingly honest. Timid, even.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.310
You said to do it "within reason"!

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:39.430
Even so, you still did it correctly.

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:42.290
You're an honest guy, for better or worse.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:45.820
From the way you act, 
I thought you'd be more of a troll.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.820
Keep up the good work!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.860
<i>He pisses me off!</i>

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:53.660
<i>Don't act like you know me! 
We only met yesterday!</i>

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:56.480
<i>And his certainty about it 
pisses me off even more!</i>

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.610
<i>You ain't even seen through 
my disguise, loser!</i>

00:14:58.610 --> 00:14:59.800
Kunieda Kei.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.420
He's a newscaster... ever heard of him?

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:05.670
<i>Is he trying to set me up?</i>

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.500
I had an interview with him recently.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:09.930
Oh?

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:12.740
<i>Seriously, what's he playing at?</i>

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:14.260
I was rude to him.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:19.880
I had a separate TV interview before him.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:22.310
A newscaster around the same age came by.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.370
He was all smiles at first.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:30.330
But when I left for a second, 
he started shouting insults at the PA,

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:32.670
and even kicked him really hard...

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:36.560
When I got back, he was all smiles again.

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:39.950
I could feel my skin crawl in disgust.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:45.830
It made me remember the people who 
treated me like vermin when I started out

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:52.030
who suddenly changed their tune 
the moment I made a name for myself.

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:56.130
I realized I still held a grudge,

00:15:56.130 --> 00:16:00.310
and I was so annoyed at my own 
pettiness that I couldn't work.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:05.110
I went to sleep in a huff, 
and then Kunieda-san came by.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:09.160
I was convinced he'd be abusing 
his underlings in private, too.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.800
I was brusque with him.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:16.240
But a PA knocked over his bag, 
and Kunieda-san smiled at him.

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:19.760
He even asked if he was okay!

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:23.450
With that well-worn, dog-eared 
inflection guide in his hand...

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:26.880
<i>You bought that act, huh? 
Wow, what a simpleton!</i>

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.400
I think he actually works really hard.

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:34.540
But I treated him badly due to 
my own foolish prejudice.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.000
I'm supposed to see him again,

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.320
but I'm not sure he'll 
forgive me if I apologize.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:40.940
You're such an asshole.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.830
If the only reason you 
apologize is to be forgiven,

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.560
you shouldn't bother.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:48.640
It means you're not really serious.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:51.190
Surprisingly sound advice 
from a scoundrel like you.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:52.690
Shut up!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.840
You're right, though.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.160
I should apologize, regardless.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.910
Okay, cut! We're all clear.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.600
Great work!

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.360
I'm sorry.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:03.040
Okay!

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:06.220
I was rude to you before.

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:09.590
I had my reasons, but I shouldn't 
have taken it out on you.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.090
At any rate, I'm sorry.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.860
<i>Check it out! He really apologized!</i>

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:18.310
Really, I wasn't offended...

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:19.410
Really?

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.770
Of course not.

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:21.900
Oh, good!

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:25.670
A friend of mine said I should apologize.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:26.940
Oh, really?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.400
<i>"Friend"? Is he talkin' about me?!</i>

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.860
<i>As if! I ain't your friend, bub!</i>

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.620
We just met recently.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:35.300
He's a bit odd, of course..

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.760
He's got such a foul mouth...

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:42.200
Yes, I'm sure you'd die before you 
said some of the things he does.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.910
Do you think so?

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.620
<i>You bastard!</i>

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:48.860
By the way, do you have that 
inflection dictionary with you today?

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:52.870
Yes. I don't need it for location work,

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:54.850
but it's a bit of a lucky charm.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:58.730
When I'm nervous before a live show, 
I like to flip through it.

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:03.850
When you're nervous, it's important 
to find comfort in routine.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:06.490
Your voice is very soothing.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.440
It's so soft and rich,

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.880
and you're articulate without being slow.

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:16.890
I guess you'd have to 
study daily to achieve that.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.890
I'm afraid I still have a lot to learn.

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.450
So do I.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:26.780
Everything I create is a long series 
of "If only I'd done this or that."

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:29.570
When I'm frustrated over 
how one project turned out,

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:32.540
the only way to clear my head 
is to start a new project.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.270
That's a great story.

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:38.170
You should have let it out 
while the cameras were rolling.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.810
Heck no.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:59.150
Here.

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:00.610
What?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.490
Sometimes I'm so engrossed in my work, 
I don't hear the doorbell.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.990
Seems a little careless...

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.790
Who's the alien, anyway?

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.790
An Earthling from the future.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.610
A descendant of humanity

00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:55.850
after they moved to other planets 
when Earth was destroyed.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:58.630
But he's all alone now.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:03.800
The sight of how many people used 
to be on Earth brings him to tears.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:05.760
That's dark.

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:10.770
Creative types do tend towards the dour.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.040
<i>This guy? Dour?</i>

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:17.470
They want to do another shoot here tomorrow.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.780
I guess I can't do any work today.

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:23.550
Doesn't it annoy you, having to bow 
to someone else's schedule,

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:28.250
letting in cameras 
and interrupting your work?

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.730
I'm sure it's inconvenient for them, too.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:33.290
Carrying all that heavy equipment around...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:36.790
Besides, I like seeing Kunieda-san.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:41.400
I always thought I was a pretty quiet guy,

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:45.120
but something about him 
just gets the words flowing.

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:48.920
He's good at listening... 
or asking questions, I guess.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:53.040
Say, Owari, do you have a girlfriend?

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.390
No way! Girls are annoying.

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:57.640
A boyfriend, then?

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:58.770
Double no!

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:02.320
What kind of person 
hates both men and women?

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:05.970
Or are you mostly just 
in love with yourself?

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:08.610
Back off!

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:11.630
Hey, watch out!

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.890
You almost hit the set!

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:14.990
Hey!

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:21.110
<i>Run your stupid mouth all you like!</i>

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:26.800
<b>Tsuzuki</b>

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:25.000
<i>You still haven't even 
realized who I really am!</i>

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:36.270
Thanks for taking time out of
 your schedules, both of you.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.720
Not at all.

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:41.030
<i>Why do I need to have dinner 
with this jerk </i>now?!

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:43.240
<i>Dammit... if the invitation 
hadn't been from my producer,</i>

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.840
<i>I'd have turned it down flat!</i>

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.280
Ushio-kun. Are things going smoothly?

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:51.090
You could come to see it 
yourself, Shitara-san.

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:53.730
I prefer to wait for the finished product.

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:57.290
I hope you won't have any complaints 
after waiting that long.

00:21:57.290 --> 00:22:00.840
Don't worry. I'm a fan of yours.

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:04.800
And I have free rein on this 
project, so I'm not worried.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.720
I'm afraid that just makes me 
even more nervous!

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:12.320
Speaking of, Kunieda-san...

00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:14.770
What made you want to be a newscaster?

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:16.870
That's quite sudden...

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:19.750
Actually, I've been wondering that for a while.

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:21.860
I just couldn't find the right time to ask.

00:22:23.060 --> 00:22:25.780
You didn't actually want to at first, right?

00:22:26.590 --> 00:22:28.530
You knew that, sir?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:30.560
Everyone knows it.

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:33.180
Everyone around the station, at least.

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:35.220
You didn't want to?

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:42.670
I originally took the test 
for a regular staff position.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:45.350
But in the final interview 
with the president,

00:22:45.350 --> 00:22:48.150
he suddenly asked if I might
 try reading the news...

00:22:48.950 --> 00:22:51.620
He saw talent in you, I suppose.

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:53.010
I wonder.

00:22:53.550 --> 00:23:00.020
When I asked him why, 
he said I had "good nasals."

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:01.520
Nasals?

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:05.220
It means that when he says a hard "g,"

00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:07.790
he sounds it a little through the nose.

00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:09.030
How, exactly?

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:13.290
It's kind of like an "ng" sound, 
though that's a bit exaggerated.

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:17.480
"Forget" becomes "for-nget" 
and "vulgar" becomes "vul-ngar".

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:19.040
Those are nasals.

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:25.370
But if the "g" comes at the start of a word, 
you just pronounce it normally.

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.700
Like "garage" or "gold".

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:29.970
Though there's a little more 
to it, of course...

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:32.050
Does any of that really matter?

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:36.780
Voices that fail to master the nasal consonant 
are a little harder on the ears.

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.400
You'd be surprised what 
a difference it makes.

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:41.140
Oh, now...

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:45.770
Excuse me a minute.

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:47.060
Go ahead and eat without me.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:50.110
Kunieda-san?

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:50.810
Yes?

00:23:50.810 --> 00:23:54.410
Why didn't you say no when they 
asked you to read the news?

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:58.330
I thought fate was trying to
 tell me something, I suppose.

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:59.410
I see.

00:23:59.730 --> 00:24:03.320
I may not really get that 
whole "nasals" thing,

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:07.920
but I do think your voice 
is very easy on the ears.

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:12.120
It's not just that you have a nice voice.

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:15.810
I suppose there's a lot of technique 
involved that a layman wouldn't understand.

00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:18.010
You really are amazing.

00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:20.680
It's nothing, really...

00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:22.970
<i>What's with this guy?!</i>

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:25.100
<i>Quit starin' at me like that!</i>

00:24:28.310 --> 00:24:32.060
<i>You never look at Owari that way...</i>

00:24:32.510 --> 00:24:34.490
<i>Wait, what am I thinking?!</i>

00:24:34.490 --> 00:24:35.530
Kunieda-san?

00:24:36.710 --> 00:24:37.850
Are you all right?

00:24:37.850 --> 00:24:39.930
Oh, er...

00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:42.700
If I might ask, how have 
things been with your friend?

00:24:43.040 --> 00:24:45.610
You know, the one you mentioned before...

00:24:45.610 --> 00:24:47.980
Oh, him...

00:24:48.850 --> 00:24:50.420
I think he's mad at me.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:53.290
I said something to him... 
I didn't mean anything by it,

00:24:53.290 --> 00:24:55.250
but I think it set him off.

00:24:55.250 --> 00:24:56.640
I see...

00:24:56.960 --> 00:24:59.410
He'll be fine, though.

00:24:59.780 --> 00:25:01.770
<i>How can you be so flippant about it?!</i>

00:25:01.770 --> 00:25:03.050
<i>Try and give a crap!</i>

00:25:03.050 --> 00:25:04.940
I call him my friend, but...

00:25:05.390 --> 00:25:08.900
I really only know his 
last name and cell number.

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:12.070
The last name he gave sounded fake,

00:25:12.070 --> 00:25:14.400
but when I ask more, 
he gets mad or ignores me.

00:25:14.400 --> 00:25:18.440
I figure he doesn't want to tell me.

00:25:19.590 --> 00:25:25.160
He just barges in, 
hangs around, then leaves,

00:25:25.160 --> 00:25:28.830
like a stray cat... I never 
know what he's thinking.

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:31.830
It's strange, really...

00:25:31.830 --> 00:25:35.730
I prefer to work alone.

00:25:35.730 --> 00:25:38.680
At least, I thought I did.

00:25:38.680 --> 00:25:41.950
But when he's at my place, hanging out,

00:25:41.950 --> 00:25:47.650
flipping through a manga, 
watching TV, muttering to himself...

00:25:47.650 --> 00:25:50.090
I'm not even thinking about it,

00:25:50.090 --> 00:25:55.630
but working while I listen 
to him feels nice...

00:25:55.630 --> 00:25:57.530
it's calming.

00:26:09.420 --> 00:26:12.170
I just ate, but I'm still hungry...

00:26:20.110 --> 00:26:21.500
What?

00:26:21.500 --> 00:26:23.890
<i>Sorry about before.</i>

00:26:23.890 --> 00:26:25.730
I don't forgive you.

00:26:25.730 --> 00:26:29.070
<i>Yeah, but I still need to apologize.</i>

00:26:29.070 --> 00:26:31.230
<i>Just like you taught me.</i>

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:32.820
You're <i>really</i> pissing me off now.

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:35.400
<i>Want to stop by for some yakitori?</i>

00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:39.050
I bought some from 
the place I mentioned earlier.

00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:41.070
<b>Tanmi-ya</b>

00:26:39.050 --> 00:26:41.230
I had a good meal earlier,

00:26:41.230 --> 00:26:44.410
but I'm already hungry again.

00:26:45.410 --> 00:26:46.410
<i>What do you say?</i>

00:26:49.280 --> 00:26:50.410
Fine.

00:26:51.480 --> 00:26:52.920
Let's eat!

00:26:54.750 --> 00:26:57.600
<i>Crap! I can't eat like this...</i>

00:26:58.420 --> 00:27:01.580
Hey, what's the matter? Are you still mad?

00:27:01.970 --> 00:27:04.080
I don't want you watching me eat.

00:27:04.080 --> 00:27:05.140
Why not?

00:27:05.460 --> 00:27:08.060
I... I've got bad teeth.

00:27:08.060 --> 00:27:09.890
It's why I'm always wearing a mask.

00:27:09.890 --> 00:27:11.580
I thought you were afraid of getting sick.

00:27:11.580 --> 00:27:13.300
That's part of it, too!

00:27:13.300 --> 00:27:16.700
Just don't peek, okay? 
It'll hurt my feelings.

00:27:25.070 --> 00:27:26.410
Hey, Owari...

00:27:27.050 --> 00:27:29.310
What? Lemme eat in peace.

00:27:29.310 --> 00:27:33.430
If your teeth bother you,
 you can get them fixed.

00:27:33.430 --> 00:27:34.960
Though apparently, it hurts.

00:27:36.030 --> 00:27:37.670
It's fine.

00:27:37.670 --> 00:27:38.800
Why?

00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:41.510
If money's an issue, I'll lend you some.

00:27:41.510 --> 00:27:44.740
Or, wait... You said you had money...

00:27:44.740 --> 00:27:46.150
What are you, stupid?

00:27:46.150 --> 00:27:49.640
Don't lend money to someone you barely know.

00:27:49.640 --> 00:27:51.940
You're not just "someone," though.

00:27:53.050 --> 00:27:58.330
I'm happy to lend you money, 
because I don't care if you pay it back.

00:27:58.330 --> 00:27:59.650
I'm not taking your money.

00:27:59.650 --> 00:28:03.700
Then you're just gonna wear a mask 
for the rest of your life?

00:28:08.390 --> 00:28:09.410
Yes!

00:28:09.410 --> 00:28:13.040
I'm going to wear a mask 
for the <i>rest of my life</i>!

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:15.610
You got a problem with that?

00:28:15.610 --> 00:28:17.550
Does that <i>offend</i> you somehow?!

00:28:20.610 --> 00:28:21.830
I'm leaving.

00:28:21.830 --> 00:28:24.300
Hey! Wait!

00:28:24.300 --> 00:28:26.440
Let me go! Don't touch me!

00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:29.520
Would you chill out?!

00:28:30.040 --> 00:28:31.620
Where'd all that come from?

00:28:32.250 --> 00:28:34.250
I just decided I wanted to leave.

00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:35.330
You got a problem?

00:28:35.330 --> 00:28:38.870
Not a problem, exactly... 
I'm just asking <i>why</i>.

00:28:38.870 --> 00:28:40.990
Is it really worth getting angry about?

00:28:40.990 --> 00:28:42.150
Shut up.

00:28:42.850 --> 00:28:44.030
Just shut up!

00:28:44.030 --> 00:28:45.030
Owari!

00:28:46.130 --> 00:28:47.540
Shut up!

00:28:47.540 --> 00:28:49.240
Shut up, shut up!

00:28:50.620 --> 00:28:54.340
<i>Owari isn't my name!</i>

00:28:55.660 --> 00:28:57.660
<i>But I'm not "Kunieda-san," either...</i>

00:28:58.540 --> 00:29:00.870
<i>I don't know who I am anymore.</i>

00:29:00.870 --> 00:29:04.400
<i>Why? When did it all get so weird?</i>

00:29:05.570 --> 00:29:09.010
<i>If I hadn't met you that night...</i>

00:29:09.810 --> 00:29:11.520
<i>This is all your fault!</i>

00:29:11.880 --> 00:29:12.800
Hey...

00:29:14.130 --> 00:29:15.750
It's your fault.

00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:17.660
Okay, I'll accept that.

00:29:17.660 --> 00:29:22.930
But I can't make it right unless 
you tell me what I did wrong!

00:29:23.900 --> 00:29:27.420
Do you have that little trust in me?

00:29:27.420 --> 00:29:30.060
You can't just tell me how you really feel?

00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:33.660
If I matter so little to you, why did 
you keep coming to see me?

00:29:33.660 --> 00:29:37.080
I know I dragged you into this at first.

00:29:37.080 --> 00:29:40.380
But you kept coming after that!

00:29:40.380 --> 00:29:42.250
Even when there was no more work to do...

00:29:42.250 --> 00:29:45.750
I thought you were enjoying it. Was I wrong?

00:29:45.750 --> 00:29:47.550
I enjoyed it!

00:29:47.550 --> 00:29:52.240
I... liked it.

00:29:52.240 --> 00:29:54.060
But you don't now?

00:29:54.390 --> 00:29:56.070
No...

00:29:56.070 --> 00:30:00.380
My head's full of things 
I never thought about before.

00:30:00.960 --> 00:30:04.030
It's all your fault. It's all your fault!

00:30:04.030 --> 00:30:07.440
Explain it to me, then.

00:30:07.440 --> 00:30:08.470
No!

00:30:08.470 --> 00:30:09.450
Explain!

00:30:09.450 --> 00:30:10.530
Why?!

00:30:10.530 --> 00:30:12.480
Because I want to know!

00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:16.620
I want to really understand you!

00:30:22.570 --> 00:30:24.180
<i>His eyes are so beautiful...</i>

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:47.650
What the hell's wrong with you?! Pervert!

00:30:47.650 --> 00:30:50.160
You disgust me! Asshole!

00:31:02.130 --> 00:31:07.590
Conference Room

00:31:03.170 --> 00:31:04.500
Excuse me.

00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:12.640
<i>Asuo-san's in the hospital?</i>

00:31:12.940 --> 00:31:14.900
<i>Early-stage stomach cancer.</i>

00:31:14.900 --> 00:31:18.170
<i>Fortunately, it's entirely treatable,</i>

00:31:18.170 --> 00:31:21.970
but he'll need to focus 
on recovery for a while.

00:31:21.970 --> 00:31:29.150
So, we'd like you to pinch hit for him 
as moderator of <i>The News</i>.

00:31:29.150 --> 00:31:32.160
There's no replacement for
 Asuo Keiichi at our station.

00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:35.120
<i>His name recognition, 
his talent, his grace...</i>

00:31:35.120 --> 00:31:37.660
<i>Everyone I could choose 
is lacking something.</i>

00:31:37.660 --> 00:31:41.670
So I've decided to wager on your potential.

00:31:42.120 --> 00:31:42.880
Screw you!

00:31:42.880 --> 00:31:45.850
<i>The first broadcast 
will be a special project.</i>

00:31:45.850 --> 00:31:48.880
<i>A debate between the heads 
of the ruling and opposition parties.</i>

00:31:48.880 --> 00:31:52.490
Kunieda-kun. You've never met 
a prime minister, have you?

00:31:52.490 --> 00:31:53.680
Lucky you.

00:31:53.680 --> 00:31:55.540
You stupid asshole!

00:31:55.540 --> 00:31:57.720
I didn't ask for any of this...

00:31:57.720 --> 00:32:00.100
<b>Flush</b>

00:31:57.720 --> 00:32:00.100
You think I'm grateful to have 
that just thrown at me?

00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:03.060
There's just a month before broadcast,

00:32:03.060 --> 00:32:04.720
so we don't have time to waste.

00:32:05.070 --> 00:32:07.600
We need to get right to work.

00:32:07.600 --> 00:32:11.100
That means no more 
interviews with Tsuzuki-kun.

00:32:11.100 --> 00:32:12.820
We can send someone else to do it.

00:32:12.820 --> 00:32:15.760
<i>That's my last tie to him cut.</i>

00:32:15.760 --> 00:32:18.370
<i>I won't have to think about him anymore.</i>

00:32:18.920 --> 00:32:21.560
<i>That's a relief, at least.</i>

00:32:22.250 --> 00:32:24.090
<i>Why'd he have to freakin' kiss me?!</i>

00:32:24.090 --> 00:32:25.680
<i>It makes no damn sense!</i>

00:32:26.150 --> 00:32:29.040
<i>Plus it's been a whole day, 
and he hasn't even called!</i>

00:32:29.660 --> 00:32:32.720
<i>I might even forgive him 
if he apologized a hundred times...</i>

00:32:33.160 --> 00:32:34.680
<i>Say something already!</i>

00:32:35.920 --> 00:32:37.580
<i>These freaking people...</i>

00:32:39.220 --> 00:32:40.680
Good day, everyone.

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:43.120
I'm your moderator, Kunieda Kei.

00:32:43.120 --> 00:32:44.340
Tonight, we're...

00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:48.190
Tonight, we're... what were we doing again?

00:33:06.160 --> 00:33:08.620
<i>I have an announcement to make.</i>

00:33:07.670 --> 00:33:24.310
Newscaster Kunieda Graduates!

00:33:08.620 --> 00:33:13.670
<i>I, Kunieda, have officially 
graduated from </i>Evening File<i>.</i>

00:33:14.290 --> 00:33:16.250
<i>To everyone who's watched me 
these past two years,</i>

00:33:16.250 --> 00:33:18.800
<i>thank you for coming along for the ride.</i>

00:33:19.260 --> 00:33:23.040
<i>I can't wait to see you again 
in primetime for </i>The News<i>.</i>

00:33:27.170 --> 00:33:28.840
Congratulations, Kunieda-kun!

00:33:29.210 --> 00:33:31.860
I saw your last show from the monitors.

00:33:31.860 --> 00:33:33.760
The bouquet is a great match!

00:33:33.760 --> 00:33:35.570
Well, thank you.

00:33:35.570 --> 00:33:37.870
You're not looking well...

00:33:37.870 --> 00:33:42.210
Well, we've been working you 
hard with those meetings.

00:33:42.210 --> 00:33:44.260
It's enough to wear out even a young man.

00:33:47.030 --> 00:33:49.330
Just don't you go collapsing on us, too.

00:33:54.550 --> 00:33:57.100
Asuo Keiichi is reinventing the nightly news.

00:33:54.550 --> 00:33:57.100
I'll be filling in!

00:33:54.550 --> 00:33:57.330
<i>Meeting after meeting...</i>

00:33:57.890 --> 00:34:00.300
<i>Rehearsal, studying the news...</i>

00:34:01.120 --> 00:34:03.560
<i>I haven't had time 
for my nightly walks lately.</i>

00:34:04.320 --> 00:34:07.340
<i>That's right... I don't even have a vase.</i>

00:34:10.190 --> 00:34:11.520
Kunieda-san?

00:34:14.100 --> 00:34:16.070
What are you doing here?

00:34:16.490 --> 00:34:17.690
A vase...

00:34:17.690 --> 00:34:19.740
Do you have a vase?

00:34:19.740 --> 00:34:23.060
They gave me these flowers... 
I graduated today.

00:34:23.060 --> 00:34:25.600
But I don't have a vase at home.

00:34:25.600 --> 00:34:26.580
A vase?

00:34:27.850 --> 00:34:30.890
Oh... n-nothing. 
Forget I said anything, please.

00:34:30.890 --> 00:34:32.890
Oh, r-right!

00:34:32.890 --> 00:34:35.230
We had a big change in schedule, 
so I haven't been by.

00:34:35.230 --> 00:34:36.800
I'm so very sorry!

00:34:37.290 --> 00:34:38.800
Kunieda-san...

00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:40.610
Want to stop by my place?

00:34:40.610 --> 00:34:42.340
I do have a vase.

00:34:44.610 --> 00:34:47.800
You finished the filming and the editing?

00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:48.780
Yeah.

00:34:48.780 --> 00:34:51.390
Shitara-san just needs to look at it,

00:34:51.390 --> 00:34:54.780
and I'll do a few tweaks on my computer.

00:34:54.780 --> 00:34:56.080
I see...

00:34:56.080 --> 00:34:59.750
I guess congratulations... 
aren't quite in order yet?

00:35:00.290 --> 00:35:02.560
Aren't you the one 
deserving congratulations?

00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:06.350
You got chosen as the new host, 
right? It's incredible.

00:35:06.350 --> 00:35:09.940
It feels a little strange that the news 
show I've watched since I was a kid

00:35:09.940 --> 00:35:11.420
will be hosted by someone I know.

00:35:11.420 --> 00:35:13.970
You start tomorrow, right? Nervous?

00:35:13.970 --> 00:35:15.170
A little...

00:35:15.170 --> 00:35:19.930
But I'm sure they wouldn't have chosen you 
unless they knew you could do it.

00:35:19.930 --> 00:35:23.400
I appreciate that. 
That's what they all say...

00:35:24.650 --> 00:35:28.390
<i>Superficially, I've always 
gotten along with everyone...</i>

00:35:29.060 --> 00:35:33.430
<i>Always smiling, never getting mad 
or yelling at anyone.</i>

00:35:33.430 --> 00:35:37.060
<i>It's exhausting to speak from the heart, 
or to hear other people do it.</i>

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:42.250
<i>But if I tell him that 
I really am scared as hell...</i>

00:35:42.830 --> 00:35:44.700
<i>What would he do?</i>

00:35:44.700 --> 00:35:49.010
<i>Is now the time to remove 
the mask of Kunieda Kei,</i>

00:35:49.010 --> 00:35:51.250
<i>tied on so tightly by so many lies?</i>

00:35:51.250 --> 00:35:54.780
<i>Is now the time to tell him everything?</i>

00:35:55.420 --> 00:35:59.420
<i>Everything I've kept from him... 
Or about Owari, at last...</i>

00:36:00.850 --> 00:36:03.430
<i>This might be my last chance.</i>

00:36:03.950 --> 00:36:05.270
Um...

00:36:05.270 --> 00:36:06.050
Sorry.

00:36:06.050 --> 00:36:10.140
I know I called you by, but 
I'm actually a little busy right now.

00:36:10.140 --> 00:36:13.040
There's more I need 
to change than I thought.

00:36:13.040 --> 00:36:15.520
I need to work it all out by tomorrow.

00:36:15.520 --> 00:36:17.320
Do you mind if I focus on work?

00:36:18.380 --> 00:36:21.120
You can stay as long as you like.

00:36:31.300 --> 00:36:34.050
Reading the news and hosting a roundtable

00:36:34.050 --> 00:36:36.330
are totally different levels of difficulty.

00:36:37.040 --> 00:36:39.750
You need to know the content by heart,

00:36:39.750 --> 00:36:42.750
control the flow while keeping things light,

00:36:43.490 --> 00:36:46.800
insert little comments 
to fill a gap in conversation,

00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:49.310
and remain visible 
without stealing the show...

00:36:50.090 --> 00:36:53.160
And my first show will be 
an interparty debate.

00:36:53.160 --> 00:36:57.160
Playing traffic cop to people scrambling 
for every scrap of airtime.

00:36:58.190 --> 00:37:02.900
It sounds nice to say it was 
a flash of inspiration to choose me,

00:37:02.900 --> 00:37:04.870
but it was really just a whim.

00:37:05.570 --> 00:37:09.700
In a profession you have to win 
thousands of competitions to get ahead...

00:37:10.520 --> 00:37:12.180
Even I am just a substitute,

00:37:12.180 --> 00:37:14.710
I landed the hosting job 
of the station's flagship show.

00:37:14.710 --> 00:37:18.020
I've worked so hard, trying to beat 
out people who went for this job

00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:19.290
because they wanted it...

00:37:20.270 --> 00:37:21.580
I was always...

00:37:22.480 --> 00:37:26.210
I was... Always...

00:37:29.750 --> 00:37:31.000
Kunieda-san?

00:37:32.550 --> 00:37:34.310
It's 6 AM.

00:37:38.670 --> 00:37:40.590
I'm sorry to be a bother.

00:37:40.590 --> 00:37:44.060
No, maybe I should have woken you up.

00:37:44.060 --> 00:37:45.340
You want some coffee?

00:37:45.340 --> 00:37:47.220
No, I'd better head home.

00:37:55.060 --> 00:37:56.080
<i>Wait...</i>

00:37:57.120 --> 00:37:59.820
<i>Was the studio always this big?</i>

00:38:03.460 --> 00:38:05.670
<b>Episode 1  Special Event
 Live Studio Debate</b>

00:38:08.390 --> 00:38:10.390
<i>Forty minutes to showtime.</i>

00:38:10.390 --> 00:38:11.600
Excuse me.

00:38:12.430 --> 00:38:15.430
Can I mic you up?

00:38:16.260 --> 00:38:17.560
<i>Please, no...</i>

00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:19.100
Kunieda-san?

00:38:19.100 --> 00:38:20.690
Oh, sorry.

00:38:20.690 --> 00:38:22.880
Could I go to the restroom 
one more time first?

00:38:22.880 --> 00:38:24.940
Oh, of course!

00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:45.540
I can't run away.

00:38:47.090 --> 00:38:48.630
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:38:48.630 --> 00:38:50.430
<i>No! I can't do this!</i>

00:38:53.350 --> 00:38:54.430
Tsuzuki

00:38:59.110 --> 00:39:00.360
What?

00:39:01.430 --> 00:39:03.940
<i>I was wondering what you'd been up to.</i>

00:39:04.550 --> 00:39:07.500
<i>I made my deadline, 
so I've got some time again.</i>

00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:11.450
<i>It's about to go live, so park
 yourself in front of the TV!</i>

00:39:12.800 --> 00:39:14.000
Please help me.

00:39:15.040 --> 00:39:16.000
<i>Sure thing.</i>

00:39:16.830 --> 00:39:18.740
<i>I'll come save you right away.</i>

00:39:18.740 --> 00:39:19.830
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:39:21.420 --> 00:39:23.050
This again?

00:39:23.050 --> 00:39:25.680
You're always like this.

00:39:25.680 --> 00:39:29.930
You put up those walls and never 
tell me anything important.

00:39:30.610 --> 00:39:31.610
It's just...

00:39:32.370 --> 00:39:36.290
<i>It's just, you're the one person 
I want to understand me...</i>

00:39:36.290 --> 00:39:39.980
<i>But I also don't want you to know...</i>

00:39:40.430 --> 00:39:41.940
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:44.880
Look... the man I love once told me

00:39:44.880 --> 00:39:48.440
that when you're nervous, 
you can find comfort in routine.

00:39:49.840 --> 00:39:52.580
<i>Maybe you should try that, too.</i>

00:39:52.580 --> 00:39:54.850
<i>Anyway, be sure to watch the show!</i>

00:39:55.450 --> 00:39:57.070
What's with him?

00:39:57.070 --> 00:40:00.870
I'm suffering here, and 
he's spouting off nonsense...

00:40:20.430 --> 00:40:25.440
<b>Japanese Pronunciation
Inflection
Dictionary</b>

00:40:22.910 --> 00:40:25.100
<i>Find comfort in routine...</i>

00:40:32.220 --> 00:40:33.230
Is that...

00:40:34.330 --> 00:40:35.510
What is it?

00:40:44.080 --> 00:40:46.540
Oh... he <i>did</i> know.

00:40:46.990 --> 00:40:48.630
Kunieda-san, excuse me...

00:40:48.630 --> 00:40:50.440
Your microphone...

00:40:51.020 --> 00:40:53.700
I'm sorry. Go ahead.

00:40:53.700 --> 00:40:54.910
Here.

00:40:56.550 --> 00:41:08.060
<b>Interparty Debate Special</b>

00:40:57.030 --> 00:40:58.240
<i>Damn...</i>

00:40:58.240 --> 00:41:01.660
<i>Drawing his stupid doodles 
in a guy's work material...</i>

00:41:01.660 --> 00:41:04.020
<i>I'll give him a real piece 
of my mind when this is over!</i>

00:41:05.520 --> 00:41:07.430
Okay, we're about to roll!

00:41:07.430 --> 00:41:09.170
Five seconds to live!

00:41:09.590 --> 00:41:11.520
Four, three...

00:41:35.250 --> 00:41:37.280
<i>I hate to admit it, but I wanna see him...</i>

00:41:44.170 --> 00:41:45.060
Good evening.

00:41:45.880 --> 00:41:49.480
This is the first episode of 
the all-new <i>The News</i>.

00:41:50.320 --> 00:41:53.310
I'll be your host today, Kunieda Kei.

00:42:20.900 --> 00:42:21.760
Which are you?

00:42:23.020 --> 00:42:25.760
Kunieda-san or Owari?

00:42:29.270 --> 00:42:31.270
Half of each, I guess...

00:42:31.900 --> 00:42:33.140
I see...

00:42:34.630 --> 00:42:35.830
You're late.

00:42:35.830 --> 00:42:38.160
I was waiting so long, I fell asleep.

00:42:38.770 --> 00:42:40.780
What do you expect?

00:42:40.780 --> 00:42:43.360
We had our show post-mortem 
and preparations for tomorrow...

00:42:43.360 --> 00:42:44.740
I was busy, okay?

00:42:45.870 --> 00:42:49.090
It's funny to hear that voice 
coming from that face.

00:42:49.090 --> 00:42:50.000
Lay off!

00:42:50.600 --> 00:42:52.380
When did you realize it?

00:42:53.210 --> 00:42:54.970
"What the hell's wrong with you?!"

00:42:55.510 --> 00:42:58.760
"Pervert! You disgust me! Asshole!"

00:42:59.270 --> 00:43:00.830
Throwing that back in my face, huh?

00:43:00.830 --> 00:43:01.970
No.

00:43:01.970 --> 00:43:04.760
Well, I guess I am, a little...

00:43:05.420 --> 00:43:09.310
My mind went blank when
 you slapped me, I think.

00:43:10.270 --> 00:43:13.260
Because of that, I heard your 
voice more clearly than usual.

00:43:14.760 --> 00:43:16.030
The nasals.

00:43:16.640 --> 00:43:19.420
The way you said "g" in "wrong" 
and "disgust" were a little different.

00:43:19.420 --> 00:43:23.490
I finally realized what 
Shitara-san was talking about.

00:43:23.490 --> 00:43:27.750
Once the possibility was in 
my mind, it all fell into place.

00:43:28.320 --> 00:43:32.530
I had to wonder why I didn't see it earlier.

00:43:32.530 --> 00:43:34.860
It was so obviously you.

00:43:35.490 --> 00:43:37.010
You're not mad?

00:43:37.010 --> 00:43:38.230
Why would I be?

00:43:38.910 --> 00:43:40.790
I lied to you for so long...

00:43:40.790 --> 00:43:42.760
If I'd asked if you were the same person

00:43:42.760 --> 00:43:45.220
and you'd said no, 
that would have been a lie.

00:43:45.770 --> 00:43:47.710
But you just didn't tell me, right?

00:43:47.710 --> 00:43:49.320
And you're fine with that?

00:43:49.320 --> 00:43:51.120
Why shouldn't I be?

00:43:52.050 --> 00:43:54.600
Because it's wrong... it's mean!

00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:56.780
You must be disappointed in me.

00:43:56.780 --> 00:43:58.570
I'm not, though.

00:43:58.570 --> 00:44:00.030
Don't lie!

00:44:00.640 --> 00:44:04.440
I'm telling you I don't mind, 
so why are you mad?

00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:05.740
Because...

00:44:05.740 --> 00:44:08.070
It made me happy, actually.

00:44:10.160 --> 00:44:12.710
The prince-like Kunieda-san,

00:44:12.710 --> 00:44:15.760
and the major asshole Owari...

00:44:16.540 --> 00:44:19.020
I was falling for both of them,

00:44:19.020 --> 00:44:22.140
so this really simplifies things.

00:44:22.140 --> 00:44:24.310
You can't fall for both!

00:44:24.310 --> 00:44:26.000
But it's interesting.

00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:28.400
I know everyone has a public 
and private face...

00:44:28.400 --> 00:44:31.900
But I've never seen anyone 
take it to such extremes.

00:44:31.900 --> 00:44:34.220
Don't treat me like a lab experiment!

00:44:34.560 --> 00:44:35.520
Kei.

00:44:35.870 --> 00:44:38.800
Keep being like that. Even if it's strange...

00:44:38.800 --> 00:44:41.990
And don't show your true face

00:44:41.990 --> 00:44:43.990
to anyone but me.

00:44:44.960 --> 00:44:48.270
I never would... I'd be finished!

00:44:48.270 --> 00:44:51.500
Can I take that to mean 
you've fallen for me?

00:44:54.680 --> 00:44:56.500
Maybe... half.

00:44:57.290 --> 00:44:58.840
Half from each face?

00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:00.510
Does that add up to...

00:45:01.640 --> 00:45:02.510
Entirely?

00:45:03.340 --> 00:45:05.650
No, just half!

00:45:05.650 --> 00:45:09.730
You were half into both 
Kunieda-san and Owari, too...

00:45:10.240 --> 00:45:11.270
You're so silly.

00:45:15.830 --> 00:45:19.020
For me, it adds up to double.

00:45:29.610 --> 00:45:30.790
What now?

00:45:30.790 --> 00:45:33.760
I'm glad you have nice teeth.

00:45:33.760 --> 00:45:35.290
Of course I do—

00:45:39.850 --> 00:45:41.010
Stop!

00:45:47.100 --> 00:45:49.500
W-Wait! I don't want to!

00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:51.450
It's a little late for that!

00:45:51.450 --> 00:45:52.520
But...

00:45:52.520 --> 00:45:55.020
I just... I don't want it inside!

00:45:55.020 --> 00:45:57.520
That's not fair. You already got yours...

00:45:58.390 --> 00:46:00.460
T-Tsuzuki-san...

00:46:01.170 --> 00:46:03.270
Tsuzuki-san... I don't want this.

00:46:03.630 --> 00:46:04.780
I'm scared...

00:46:06.810 --> 00:46:09.990
You really are a nasty little creature...

00:46:12.310 --> 00:46:13.340
Ow!

00:46:14.250 --> 00:46:17.410
I'll have to beat that out of you.

00:46:17.410 --> 00:46:19.400
You said I was fine the way I was.

00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:21.650
Not literally all the time!

00:46:21.650 --> 00:46:23.520
Do you really delight in tormenting me?

00:46:23.520 --> 00:46:25.110
You're the one who—

00:46:25.520 --> 00:46:26.950
I said no!

00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:29.620
You've half-convinced me.

00:46:29.620 --> 00:46:31.280
So I'll only put it in halfway.

00:46:31.280 --> 00:46:33.010
That's not much of a difference!

00:46:33.010 --> 00:46:34.610
Shut up.

00:46:34.610 --> 00:46:36.290
I love you, so shut your mouth.

00:46:36.290 --> 00:46:37.710
I don't want this!

00:46:37.710 --> 00:46:39.960
Ow, it hurts! It hurts!

00:46:41.490 --> 00:46:42.920
Sorry.

00:46:42.920 --> 00:46:44.780
Oh, well...

00:46:46.050 --> 00:46:49.080
You can't fool me again!

00:46:49.080 --> 00:46:51.010
The pain is real, though!

00:46:51.010 --> 00:46:53.300
It'll hurt more if you struggle.

00:46:53.300 --> 00:46:56.750
Breathe... slow and deep...

00:46:59.030 --> 00:47:01.450
A-Are you in halfway yet?

00:47:01.450 --> 00:47:03.020
Not yet...

00:47:05.250 --> 00:47:06.920
N-No...

00:47:08.560 --> 00:47:11.180
Kei... Kei!

00:47:12.760 --> 00:47:15.660
I'm sorry... I can't stop myself.

00:47:24.510 --> 00:47:27.950
L-Liar... You said... only halfway...

00:47:27.950 --> 00:47:30.990
But... you put the whole thing in...

00:47:30.990 --> 00:47:33.450
Yeah, you got me...

00:47:33.450 --> 00:47:36.400
I think I'm just swept away 
by your beauty...

00:47:36.400 --> 00:47:37.740
Oh, stow it!

00:47:38.330 --> 00:47:40.750
I'll take it slow.

00:47:44.690 --> 00:47:47.260
Crap. This sucks...

00:47:48.110 --> 00:47:52.260
When I remember this, I won't 
be able to go anywhere else...

00:47:54.360 --> 00:47:55.700
Stupid...

00:48:02.270 --> 00:48:05.270
<b>Show Ratings
 The News</b>

00:48:02.270 --> 00:48:05.270
<b>Revamp First Episode 
Average Rating: 
23.5%
Celebrate! High ratings!
We took our timeslot!</b>

00:48:06.580 --> 00:48:07.620
Kunieda!

00:48:08.950 --> 00:48:10.400
Good morning.

00:48:10.720 --> 00:48:12.440
I've been looking for you.

00:48:12.440 --> 00:48:14.340
Sure, putting him on now.

00:48:18.320 --> 00:48:19.690
Hello?

00:48:19.690 --> 00:48:22.590
<i>Good morning. Great work last night.</i>

00:48:22.590 --> 00:48:24.500
A-Asuo-san?

00:48:24.500 --> 00:48:26.790
<i>I'm sorry to burden you with all that.</i>

00:48:26.790 --> 00:48:28.000
No, not at all...

00:48:28.610 --> 00:48:31.290
<i>You kept the show going smoothly.</i>

00:48:31.630 --> 00:48:34.320
<i>I can't wait to see where 
you go next, Kunieda.</i>

00:48:34.730 --> 00:48:36.260
I appreciate that.

00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:38.060
<i>I've got high hopes.</i>

00:48:38.060 --> 00:48:40.800
<i>Of course, I would've done it better.</i>

00:48:41.880 --> 00:48:45.580
I'd planned to take it easy for a while, 
but I've changed my mind.

00:48:46.630 --> 00:48:48.780
I'm coming back as soon as I can.

00:48:50.480 --> 00:48:52.940
I'll be happy to see you then, Asuo-san.

00:52:28.820 --> 00:52:30.940
Sports is up next.

00:52:30.940 --> 00:52:33.060
Minagawa-san, over to you.

00:52:33.040 --> 00:52:52.890
<i>Locker Room</i>

00:52:33.060 --> 00:52:34.020
Right!

00:52:34.020 --> 00:52:35.930
Let's talk about baseball!

00:52:35.930 --> 00:52:40.370
I, Minagawa Tatsuki, will interview 
the player who brought his team to victory

00:52:37.090 --> 00:52:52.890
<b>Minagawa Tatsuki</b>

00:52:40.370 --> 00:52:44.350
with a come-from-behind home run!

00:52:44.830 --> 00:52:47.280
It's an exclusive interview with <i>The News</i>!

00:52:47.930 --> 00:52:50.020
You won't want to miss it!

00:52:54.230 --> 00:52:58.070
The End
